// An unknown service name has two ways into a table, and both have to be
// reported against the field that holds them: the `kind` a provider supplies,
// and an entry of the `required_services` a house asks for.
//
// **Why this is two rows and used to be one.** Until phase 14.4 a single
// "temple" carried both — it declared a service *and* required some — because
// nothing stopped it: the shape was flat and the classification was inferred
// from what was missing. A row now says which of the two it is, and a provider
// that also requires services is `RequirementsOnAProvider`. Keeping the one-row
// version would have made this fixture report a third error it is not about, so
// it says the same thing with one row each.
(
    buildings: [
        (
            id: "temple",
            size: (1, 1),
            cost: 30,
            levels: 1,
            role: "provider",
            service: Some((kind: "astral_transport", range_per_level: [5], capacity_per_level: [5])),
        ),
        (
            id: "house",
            size: (1, 1),
            cost: 10,
            levels: 1,
            role: "house",
            required_services: ["ambrosia"],
        ),
    ],
)
